      "content": "While your intention to avoid unnecessary expenses and doctor visits is understandable, it may not be wise to try and self-treat an undiagnosed skin condition. Red post marks on your skin, if indeed referring to ringworm, can be symptomatically similar, but it's also important to consider all possibilities. Self-treatment might only exacerbate the issue or delay proper treatment. The longer waiting time for an appointment may help you incorrectly classify a potentially more serious condition. Please consider at least trying over-the-counter options, and if symptoms persist or worsen, see a medical professional for accurate diagnosis and treatment. Timely professional guidance is often cost-effective in the long run due to preventing complications.\n\nRemember, a healthcare professional's advice is necessary when it comes to medical conditions, and self-care should not replace professional diagnosis and treatment. Given your busy schedule and concern about expenses, perhaps you could consider booking an appointment with a walk-in clinic or using telemedicine options; these might provide more flexibility. Take care of your health, and don't delay when it comes to potentially skin infections or allergic reactions.",
